  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1043 PM CDT WED OCT 21 2026\n\nDry and very pleasant weather continues the next 7 days. Mid-\nlevel ridging builds eastward over the area the next couple days.\nA cold air damming (CAD) wedge builds in Friday through the\nweekend in the wake of Subtropical Storm Josephine, resulting in\nslightly cooler high temperatures over the weekend. High\ntemperatures trend upward slightly next week as the wedge weakens\nand a weakening shortwave trough and front approach the area. With\nlittle to no moisture return due to persistent high pressure at\nthe surface, the forecast remains dry next week.\n\n32/JDavis",
